This project is an independent Rust implementation of ideas published in

  W. Thomason, Z. Kingston, L. E. Kavraki,
  "Motions in Microseconds via Vectorized Sampling-Based Planning", ICRA 2024.
  https://github.com/KavrakiLab/vamp (Apache-2.0)

No VAMP source code is included. The following third-party data is used:

* crates/motionamigo/robots/panda.toml: the collision sphere decomposition of the Franka Emika Panda is
  derived from resources/panda/panda_spherized.urdf in the VAMP repository
  (Apache-2.0, Copyright Kavraki Lab, Rice University), which in turn originates from
  robowflex_resources (https://github.com/KavrakiLab/robowflex_resources, MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2020 Kavraki Lab). The self-collision pairs are derived from the
  panda.srdf in the same repositories.
* crates/motionamigo/robots/ur5.toml: the collision sphere decomposition of the Universal
  Robots UR5 with a Robotiq 2F-85 gripper is derived from resources/ur5/ur5_spherized.urdf in
  the VAMP repository (Apache-2.0, Copyright Kavraki Lab, Rice University), which in turn
  originates from robowflex_resources (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 Kavraki Lab). The
  self-collision pairs are derived from the ur5.srdf in the same repositories. The standard DH
  parameters of the UR5 are taken from the public Universal Robots documentation.
* The Denavit-Hartenberg parameters and joint limits of the Panda are taken from the
  public Franka robot documentation.
* bench/vamp/: scripts that download the MotionBenchMaker problem set shipped with VAMP
  at benchmark time. The problem files are not redistributed in this repository.
